#. i18n: file: functions/text.xml:240
#: xml_doc.cpp:4536
msgid ""
"The FIND() function finds one text string (find_text) within another text "
"string (within_text) and returns the number of the starting point of "
"find_text, from the leftmost character of within_text."
msgstr ""
"Die Soek() funksie vind een teks string (find_text) binne in nog 'n teks "
"string (within_text) en gee terug Die nommer van Die beginne punt van "
"find_text, van Die mees linkse karakter van within_text."

#. i18n: file: functions/text.xml:241
#: xml_doc.cpp:4538
msgid ""
"Parameter start_num specifies the character at which to start the search. "
"The first character is character number 1. If start_num is omitted, it is "
"assumed to be 1."
msgstr ""
"Parameter start_num spesifiseer die karakter na wat na begin die soektog. "
"die eerste karakter is karakter nommer 1. As start_num is weggelaat, dit is "
"aangeneem na wees 1."

#. i18n: file: functions/text.xml:242
#: xml_doc.cpp:4540
msgid ""
"You can also use function SEARCH, but unlike SEARCH, FIND is case-sensitive "
"and does not allow wildcard characters."
msgstr ""
"Jy kan asook gebruik funksie Soektog, maar ander as Soektog, Soek is case-"
"sensitive en doen nie toelaat willekeurige karakter karakters."

#. i18n: file: functions/text.xml:243
#: xml_doc.cpp:4542
msgid "FIND(find_text;within_text;start_num)"
msgstr "Soek(find_text;within_text;start_num)"

#. i18n: file: functions/text.xml:244
#: xml_doc.cpp:4544
msgid "FIND(\"KOf\";\"KOffice\") returns 1"
msgstr "Soek(\"Kof\";\"Koffice\") gee terug 1"

